# Everything in this repository is stored with LF, and is checked out with LF
# too, on every platform.
#
# Without the `eol=lf` half, Git on Windows honours core.autocrlf and hands the
# working tree CRLF files. Prettier is configured with `endOfLine: 'lf'`, so it
# then reports those files as unformatted - `npm run format:check` fails locally
# while the same check passes in CI, where the checkout is LF. Pinning the
# checkout removes that split.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone, which
# covers the node icons.
* text=auto eol=lf
